raw.job_description:
Join the team building an AI-first company.

Hostinger serves more than 5.5 million clients across 150 countries, but we're still excited about what we're creating next.

AI is changing how we build products, support customers, work together, and solve problems. It helps us move faster, spend less time on repetitive work, and focus on bigger ideas.

If you want your work to influence both what we build and how we build it, we'd like to meet you.

Our culture:

Guided by 10 company principles.

Your role at Hostinger

Join Hostinger's Product team as SysAdmins Manager and lead the Web Hosting SysAdmin team in Indonesia. The team keeps more than 1,600 bare-metal hosting servers across 16+ data centres healthy and covers the Asia‑Pacific daytime window of our 24/7 global rotation, working hand in hand with the Lithuanian and Brazilian SysAdmin teams.

This is a hands‑on technical leadership role. About half of your time stays technical: you operate, debug and ship alongside your engineers. The other half goes into your people: hiring, coaching, protecting the team's health and setting them up to succeed.

You own the team's shift coverage and incident response, but you are not personally on rotation or on‑call. You will work closely with engineering, developer, Customer Success and product managers.

Curious to learn more? Connect with your team: Teodoras Celencevičius

Your day-to-day

• Lead the Indonesian Web Hosting SysAdmin team and own its shift coverage: you design the rotation, you are not on it;

• Own incident response in your window: acknowledgement, customer communication, postmortems and follow‑up within SLA;

• Act as the sysadmin escalation point for Customer Success on complex hosting and security cases;

• Stay hands‑on across a fleet running CloudLinux, LiteSpeed, cPanel/WHM and MariaDB: diagnose, optimise and fix;

• Deliver long‑term engineering and automation with Ansible/AWX, Prometheus and Grafana that removes repetitive shift work;

• Drive AI adoption in operations: automated ticket resolution, AI‑assisted diagnosis and faster runbooks;

• Hire, onboard and coach; run weekly reporting, team KPIs and quarterly performance reviews;

• Coordinate daily with the Lithuanian and Brazilian SysAdmin teams, WH engineering and product, and make the final technical call when the team needs one.

What will help you succeed

• You have 3+ years supporting enterprise‑scale Linux environments, including database and web‑server performance tuning;

• You have 1+ years leading or mentoring an engineering or sysadmin team, ideally one that runs shifts or on‑call;

• You have hands‑on experience with the web hosting stack: cPanel/WHM, LiteSpeed, Apache or Nginx, MariaDB/MySQL, CloudLinux (LVE, CageFS);

• You understand on‑premises / bare‑metal infrastructure;

• You are comfortable with security hardening and malware response on shared hosting (Imunify360, Monarx or similar);

• You script and automate: Bash or Python, Ansible;

• You have hired before and know what a strong sysadmin looks like in an interview;

• Your English skills are C1 - C2;

• You are a constant learner who loves Linux and cares about uptime, people and clean processes.

Meet your team

The Web Hosting SysAdmin team keeps the infrastructure behind Hostinger's hosting services healthy, stable, and ready to support millions of customers worldwide. We are distributed across Indonesia, Lithuania and Brazil, which gives us round‑the‑clock coverage and expertise from three markets.

Each location has its own team and manager, but we work as one: shared runbooks, shared incidents, shared goals. In Indonesia, you will lead an experienced sysadmin team who care deeply about Linux and about making our hosting environment better every week.

Benefits you'll love

• 360 Growth: We provide limitless learning opportunities: access to platforms like Reforge and CoachHub, global conferences, feedback culture, digital libraries, and industry‑leading subscriptions. Advance your career with internal mobility, and grow with a team eager to share knowledge and support your success.

• Freedom & responsibility: Work on your terms, whether from the comfort of home or anywhere in the world. With a home office budget, you can elevate your workspace. Enjoy the flexibility to manage your schedule while bringing your ideas to life in a fast‑paced, dynamic environment.

• Wellness simplified: Your health comes first with company‑provided sick days, 20 paid suspension days, Headspace subscriptions, and recharge leave. Participate in wellbeing‑dedicated events and simply enjoy the balance of a lifestyle that prioritizes wellness.

• Work hard - play hard: Celebrate your achievements with company events like Town Hall, Meet the Client initiatives, team‑building experiences, and workations. Celebrate life’s big moments with milestone gifts for weddings, new parenthood, and graduations.

Compensation

Salary depending on your experience and skills.

Get ready to take your personal and professional growth to new heights! Join Hostinger today and be part of our journey.

Three. Two. Onboard.

Requirements:

Minimal S1 dari jurusan Teknik Informatika/Ilmu Komputer/Sistem Informasi/Teknik Elektro, atau jurusan terkait bidang IT;
Diutamakan berpengalaman sebagai Programmer/System Support/System Analyst/Quality Assurance/Quality Control minimal 3 tahun;
Memahami konsep database aplikasi, software requirements, software design, software development fundamentals, software development process, software debugging, software documentation, dan software testing;
Memahami bahasa pemrograman web berbasis Java atau PHP serta bahasa pemrograman web lain pendukungnya seperti HTML, XML, Javascript, CSS, JSON, Play Framework, CodeIgniter Framework atau Yii Framework;
Memahami konsep dan teknik interkoneksi antarsistem menggunakan web service;
Memiliki kemampuan problem solving yang baik, komunikasi yang baik, kreativitas/inisiatif tinggi, dapat bekerja dalam tim/individu, mampu bekerja di bawah tekanan.

📩 Apply sekarang dengan mengirimkan CV ke:👉 https://lnkd.in/gkqQpQhY

Kami sedang mencari UI/UX Designer yang kreatif dan berbakat untuk bergabung dengan Techarea. Sebagai UI/UX Designer, Anda akan memainkan peran penting dalam mengubah ide-ide dan konsep menjadi antarmuka pengguna yang menarik dan fungsional.

Tugas dan Kewajiban:

• Menyiapkan storyboards, alur proses, atau sitemap untuk memberikan pandangan holistik tentang desain.

• Merancang wireframe yang akan menjadi dasar untuk pengembangan antarmuka pengguna.

• Merancang antarmuka pengguna yang konsisten, fungsional, mudah dikembangkan, dan memikat secara visual.

• Membuat mockup dan prototipe yang mencerminkan fungsionalitas desain.

• Melakukan iterasi desain hingga mencapai desain yang optimal.

• Bekerja sama secara erat dengan tim developer untuk mengoordinasikan proses handoff desain.

Kualifikasi:

• Memahami prinsip-prinsip desain dan praktik terbaik desain UI.

• Memahami prinsip-prinsip UX dan dapat membuat desain UI untuk berbagai perangkat.

• Memahami istilah-istilah dalam bahasa Inggris terkait desain UI/UX.

• Memiliki pengetahuan mendalam dan kemampuan menggunakan aplikasi desain UI/UX.

• Kemampuan bekerja secara mandiri dan berkolaborasi dalam tim.

• Proaktif dan responsif dalam berkomunikasi dengan tim, serta mampu memberikan dan menerima umpan balik dengan konstruktif.

• Pendidikan minimal SMK bidang Teknologi dan Rekayasa, Teknologi Informasi, atau bidang terkait, dengan pengalaman minimal 1 tahun sebagai UI/UX Designer.

