Job Description
• Collecting data from various sources, including financial reports, operational metrics, sales data, and customer feedback;
• Data Quality Assurance: Ensuring the accuracy, completeness, and reliability of data used for analysis;
• Managing data organization to ensure data is organized and easily accessible;
• Developing and monitoring KPIs to measure business performance across various functions;
• Designing and maintaining dashboards that provide real-time visibility into business performance metrics;
• Generating regular performance reports for stakeholders, highlighting key findings and trends.
• Trend Analysis: Identifying trends and patterns in business performance data to inform strategic decisions;
• Bench marking: Comparing the company’s performance against industry standards and competitors;
• Statistical Analysis: Using statistical methods to analyze data and draw meaningful insights.
• Process Efficiency: Analyzing business processes to identify inefficiencies and recommend improvements;
• Resource Utilization: Evaluating the utilization of resources, including manpower, equipment, and materials;
• Productivity Metrics: Measuring and analyzing productivity to identify opportunities for operational improvement.

Job Requirements
• Minimal 2 years of working experience in Data Analytics, especially in P&L analysis.
• Strong exposure in excel skills & data visualization with power BI.
• Able to work under pressure, has good interpersonal & communication skill.
• Willing to work fully from office (Placement in West Jakarta office).

We’re an early stage tech startup in the artificial intelligence space, already working with global institutions who utilize our products today. After launching and scaling quickly, we’re now focused on making certain our platform is even more intuitive, seamless, and human-centered. To help us on that journey, we’re looking for a UI/UX Design Manager who’s excited to be both hands‑on in design execution and a leader in shaping our future design team.

What You’ll Do:
• Act as a player-coach: designing wireframes, mockups, and prototypes in Figma while also guiding the broader design vision;
• Work closely with engineers, product managers, and executives to transform complex, AI-driven workflows into simple, elegant user experiences;
• Work closely with executives and the marketing team to ensure our designs and marketing materials align;
• Build and maintain a scalable design system to unify our platform as it grows;
• Run user research and usability testing to ground design decisions in real customer needs;
• Lay the foundation for a future design team—mentoring others and helping us hire as we scale;
• Balance speed with craft: you’ll ship quickly without compromising usability and polish;
• Detail-oriented, Team Player is an absolute must.

You must understand design principles and be able to build designs without the help of AI and use AI to enhance your own designs.
